## STEP A — LOAD THE CONTRACT (mandatory)

0. **Check which course you're forging before assuming a JSON exists.**
   FE I has one. **FE II does not** — `unicrawler`'s portal probe
   (2026-07-28) returned *"Subject 'Desarrollo Web: Front-End II' not
   found in UDIT portal study"* (`desarrollo-web-front-end-ii-2025-2026-NOT-FOUND.md`,
   same directory), an honest negative result, not a parser failure. This
   is a **separate** institutional gap from the already-tracked FE II PDF
   `TEMARIO`/bibliography clerical error
   (`2026-27-syllabus-renewal-plan.md` §1, in progress) — don't conflate
   the two, and don't assume fixing one fixes the other. For FE II:
   skip to A.6; there is no JSON to parse in A.1–A.5. State this
   explicitly in the forged CV's own text (see the editorial-note pattern
   in `cv/udit-ruvebal-frontend-ii-cv.md`'s Objetivos section, added
   2026-08-18) — do not silently draft as if a JSON authority exists.
1. **(FE I only)** Parse GUIDE_JSON. Copy identity fields
   (`subject_name`, `ects`, `semester`, `academic_year`,
   `coordinating_professor`, `source_url`) verbatim.
2. **(FE I only)** Extract `contents` → CONTENIDOS anchor list. Do not
   drop or reorder silently; show the mapping table if you cluster for
   pedagogy.
3. **(FE I only)** List `competencies` exactly as strings in the JSON —
   `CN03`, `HB02`, `HB05`, `HB06`, `CM01` as of the 2025-2026 guide. **For
   FE II**, these same codes likely apply (probably a degree-level
   catalog, shared across subjects — unconfirmed without an official FE II
   source) but the *descriptions* must describe FE II's own content, not
   be copied from FE I's. Getting this wrong once already cost a real
   edit — see the note above.
4. **(FE I only)** Load `formative_activities` — hours must sum to **150**
   at the 10/30/14/94/2 split (`fe-unit-forge.mdc` §1's table, quoted
   verbatim there from the official text — Lección Magistral /
   Prácticas de Laboratorio / Resolución de Ejercicios / Estudio autónomo
   / Evaluación). If they don't sum to 150, stop: the clone is stale,
   re-check the live PDF. **For FE II**, this hour split is still
   binding (`institution-fe.md`'s hour-scheme table) even without a JSON
   — it's the one part of the contract independently confirmed correct
   in the live PDF (`2026-27-syllabus-renewal-plan.md` §1: "`ACTIVIDADES
   FORMATIVAS` ... are correct, on-topic").
5. **(FE I only)** Load `evaluation` — weights must match JSON **and** the
   live PDF. Sum must be 100%. **For FE II**, use the live PDF's
   evaluation section directly (per §1, it's correct) — do not invent
   weights, and do not silently reuse FE I's if they differ.
6. Ground any research/pedagogy claims via the evidence matrix in
   [`grounding/README.mdc`](./grounding/README.mdc) — read **this unit's
   row**, authoritative over priors. Only Ahmes `--cite` with
   `evaluator_safe=yes` may enter published bibliography lines.
   `[BIBLIO-GAP]` stays labelled, never silently repaired.

